<title>UK: British beet test shows 77.1 grams sugar per root.</title>
<headline>British beet test shows 77.1 grams sugar per root.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of the fourth British sugar beet test, carried out on Tuesday August 27 and issued by British Sugar Plc.</p>
<p>			   4TH TEST 96  4TH TEST 95    5-YR AVG</p>
<p> SUGAR GRAMS/ROOT	  77.1	   80.7	    86.8</p>
<p> SUGAR CONTENT (PCT)    15.48	  18.54	   16.82</p>
<p> ROOT WEIGHT (GRAMS)	498	    435	     516</p>
<p>&quot;The crop has maintained an average growth rate and continues to be on course for an average result, helped by recent rainfall,&quot; said a spokesman for British Sugar.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
